window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"quinn","b":"locke","win":["Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 1","text":"Your Q outranges everything Locke has, and the blind switches off his Silver Stake autos — pressure from the first wave is yours."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"Vault adds a dash-reset and a second blind; every short trade you start is now won before he answers."},{"when":"Locke level 6","text":"Purgatory turns your low HP into an execute after a slow-in — the free lane ends the moment he hits 6."},{"when":"Locke first item","text":"His burst plus the totem execute now kills from deceptively high HP; respect every all-in attempt."}],"wants":{"you":["Harrier poke every time he steps to farm","Vault held to break his E dash","HP above execute range after his 6"],"foe":["A slow-in that lands Purgatory","To catch you with Vault down","Extended trades inside auto range"]},"early":"Levels 1 through 5 are yours: Q blind shuts off his Silver Stake autos, Harrier marks chunk him at every last hit, and level-3 Vault hands you a dash-reset plus a second blind. Keep your Q and E cycling ahead of his gap-close and he never completes a full trade — build the CS and HP lead now.","mid":"At 6 the lane evens, and at his first item it tilts his way: after a slow-in, Purgatory executes you below threshold, so stop coin-flipping at half HP. Shove with your poke lead and convert your movement speed into roams — you beat this Locke on the map, not inside his all-in window.","late":"Two-plus items is a genuine coinflip: his single-target burst is real, but Valor disengage offsets it as long as you are never caught alone below execute range. Kite fights from the edge, save the blind for his key damage window, and keep turning roam speed into cross-map picks and objectives.","whys":["Your level-1 Q outranges him and the blind shuts off his Silver Stake autos — the opening trades are yours.","At 2, Harrier marks plus Q poke chunk him every single time he steps up to farm.","Level 3 Vault gives you a dash-reset and a second blind, winning any trade you choose to take.","Through 4-5 your Q and E cooldowns stay ahead of his gap-close, so you keep kiting him off you for free.","At 6 it evens out: his all-in threat comes online and forces you to start respecting his engage windows.","Once his first item lands, Purgatory lets him totem-execute you below threshold after a slow-in — his stage.","Post-items it is a skill coinflip: your Valor disengage offsets his burst if you space the execute range."]});
