window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"quinn","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Zaahen level 2","text":"His trade tools come online and out-value your poke-and-reset pattern — stop taking trades that look free."},{"when":"Levels 4-5","text":"Your range and Vault resets finally stabilise the lane; farm cleanly and dodge his commits."},{"when":"Your level 6","text":"Behind Enemy Lines is your out — it wins the map while his R only wins the lane."},{"when":"Zaahen first item","text":"His item bricks your falloff damage; from here he can simply walk you down in lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Short poke, never extended trades","Roams on 6 before his item spike","The game closed before two items"],"foe":["Extended trades your resets cannot refund","A stat-check duel after first item","A long game where he outsustains you"]},"early":"Level 1 is an even farming stage, then his 2-3 window bites: his Q and E win any extended trade that your short cooldowns cannot refund. Poke on his approach, back off before the answer comes, and lean on levels 4-5 — where range and Vault resets stabilise things — to farm safely and dodge his commits.","mid":"Level 6 stays even because your R is a roam tool rather than the all-in flip his is — so use it that way. Shove the wave and run Behind Enemy Lines to hit other lanes while he is stuck pushing. Once his first item bricks your falloff damage, stop contesting him head-on entirely and play for tempo.","late":"Two items in, he outstats and outsustains you — you are a lane bully with nothing left in the duel. Hold sidelane vision, kite his walk-downs with Vault and the blind, and cash your mobility in for picks, objectives, and cross-map plays before he ever gets to force the 1v1 he wants.","whys":["Level 1 is an even skill lane before ults and item stats matter to either of you.","At 2 his early trade tools already out-value your poke-and-reset pattern — his stage.","By 3 The Darkin Glaive and Aureate Rush win extended trades your cooldowns cannot refund — keep it brief.","Levels 4-5 are close: your range and Vault resets let you farm and dodge his commits.","Level 6 reads even — your R is a roam tool, not the all-in flip his is, and neither pops the lane open here.","His first item bricks your falloff damage and lets him start walking you down — respect the spike.","With two items he outstats and outsustains you; the duel belongs to him, so stop offering it."]});
