window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"quinn","b":"masteryi","win":["Quinn","Quinn","Quinn","Skill","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Level 1","text":"Blinding Assault erases his autos and Vault leaps you to max range — he has no answer yet."},{"when":"Level 3","text":"You fully control the spacing with Vault and poke; deny him every wave you safely can."},{"when":"Yi 6 + first item","text":"Highlander plus an item lets him finally stick to you — the free lane is over."},{"when":"Yi two items","text":"With resets online he deletes you on contact; never sidelane or face-check without backup."}],"wants":{"you":["The blind saved for his biggest DPS window","Vault the instant he commits","A big early lead cashed before his spike"],"foe":["A quiet farm lane into first item","Highlander flanks you cannot kite","Reset chains through your backline"]},"early":"You own the first three levels outright: Blinding Assault erases his autos, Vault leaps you clear on 12s, and Meditate is a channel your Vault interrupt cancels outright. Chunk him at each last hit and call jungle pressure — the lead you build here is the only currency that matters against a scaling Yi.","mid":"Levels 4-5 hinge on your Q blind and Vault timing, and 6 stays even since your ult is a roam tool rather than a duel button. So roam: shove waves, hit other lanes with your speed, and force the map to crumble around him while he is still farming his way toward the Highlander spike.","late":"From his first item onward, Highlander's slow immunity lets him stick to you and you are the squishy target he hunts. Never sidelane alone, hold the blind for his commit, and bring Grievous Wounds for Meditate — you win by making every fight team-sized instead of Yi-sized.","whys":["Blinding Assault erases his autos and Vault leaps you clear — level 1 is yours.","Q blind and constant kiting keep him off you through level 2 — he cannot reach you.","At 3 you still control the spacing with Vault and poke; every trade starts on your terms.","Wuju Style adds true damage, so armour will not save a fumbled Vault — clean cooldown usage is the stage.","Level 6 is even because your R is a roam tool, not a duel tool — neither of you flips the lane here.","His first item plus Highlander lets him finally stick to and kill you — the kill pressure is his now.","With R resets and item power he deletes you and your team late; only group play answers it."]});
